6. Full Historical Claim Specification
6.1 Historical Claim Schema
The historical claim schema defines the structure of a historical claim deposit.

It has the following fields:

claim_id. A string. Required.

claim_name. A string. Required.

claim_description. A string. Required.

period. An object. Required. It contains start_date and end_date.

region. An array of strings. Required.

subjects. An array of strings. Required.

claim_type. An enum. Required. The values are event, cause, process, trend, attribution, interpretation, other.

contested_status. An enum. Required. The values are uncontested, contested, disputed, refuted, uncertain.

evidence_for. An array of evidence objects. Required.

evidence_against. An array of evidence objects. Optional.

revisions. An array of revision objects. Optional.

historians. An array of historian objects. Optional.

key_dates. An array of date objects. Optional.

key_figures. An array of figure objects. Optional.

related_claims. An array of claim relations. Optional.

evidence_strength. An enum. Required. The values are strong, moderate, weak, not_assessed.

provenance. An object. Required.

stag_annotation. An object. Optional.

work_reference. A string. Optional.

keywords. An array of strings. Optional.

notes. A string. Optional.

moderation_status. An enum. The values are pending, approved, rejected.

version. An integer.

supersedes. A string. Optional.

superseded_by. A string. Optional.

Each evidence object has:

evidence_id. A string.

evidence_type. An enum. The values are primary_source, secondary_source, artefact, testimony, data, other.

source_reference. A string.

source_summary. A string.

source_date. A string in ISO8601 format. Optional.

reliability. An enum. The values are high, medium, low, unknown.

notes. A string. Optional.

Each revision object has:

revision_id. A string.

revision_date. A string in ISO8601 format.

revision_description. A string.

previous_position. A string.

new_position. A string.

historian_id. A string. Optional.

notes. A string. Optional.

Each historian object has:

historian_id. A string.

historian_name. A string.

historian_position. An enum. The values are supports, opposes, neutral, uncertain.

historian_school. A string. Optional.

Each date object has:

date_id. A string.

date_value. A string in ISO8601 format.

date_description. A string.

reliability. An enum. The values are high, medium, low, unknown.

Each figure object has:

figure_id. A string.

figure_name. A string.

figure_role. An enum. The values are participant, source, historian, other.

figure_description. A string.

Each claim relation has:

relation_id. A string.

related_claim_id. A string.

relation_type. An enum. The values are same_period, same_region, cause, consequence, related, independent.

relation_note. A string. Optional.

