7. Core Logic as Executable Pseudocode
7.1 Create Historical Claim
function createHistoricalClaim(claim, files, provenance, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "depositor"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Validate the claim against the schema. If invalid, return an error with the details.

Step 3. If the STAG annotation is present, validate it.

Step 4. If the work reference is present, look it up. If null, flag it as unresolved.

Step 5. Generate a claim ID. Set the fields: version 1, moderation_status pending, deposit_date now, depositor_id from auth, depositor_affiliation from auth, provenance from provenance.

Step 6. Insert the historical claim.

Step 7. Insert the evidence records, the revision records, the historians, the key dates, the key figures, and the claim relations.

Step 8. Insert the STAG link and the work link if present.

Step 9. Insert the provenance.

Step 10. Insert the moderation record.

Step 11. Insert the audit log entry.

Step 12. Return the claim_id and the status created.

7.2 Read Historical Claim
function readHistoricalClaim(claimId, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "reader"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read the claim. If null, return an error.

Step 3. Read the evidence, the revisions, the historians, the key dates, the key figures, the relations, the links, the provenance, and the moderation.

Step 4. Reconstruct the deposit.

Step 5. Insert the audit log entry.

Step 6. Return the deposit.

7.3 Update Historical Claim
function updateHistoricalClaim(claimId, claim, provenance, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "depositor"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read the existing claim. If null, return an error.

Step 3. Validate the new claim.

Step 4. Increment the version. Update the supersedes and superseded_by fields.

Step 5. Insert a provenance record with operation update.

Step 6. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 7. Return the claim_id, the version, and the status updated.

7.4 Delete Historical Claim
function deleteHistoricalClaim(claimId, provenance, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "admin"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read the existing claim. If null, return an error.

Step 3. If soft delete, mark as deleted. Otherwise, remove.

Step 4. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 5. Return the claim_id and the status deleted.

7.5 Query Historical Claims
function queryHistoricalClaims(query, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "reader"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Build and execute the query.

Step 3. Read the matching claims.

Step 4. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 5. Return the claims, the count, and the pagination.

7.6 Aggregate Historical Claims
function aggregateHistoricalClaims(query, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "reader"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Build and execute the aggregation.

Step 3. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 4. Return the results.

7.7 Full-Text Search
function fullTextSearch(query, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "reader"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Build and execute the search.

Step 3. Read the matching claims.

Step 4. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 5. Return the claims and the count.

7.8 Export Historical Claim
function exportHistoricalClaim(claimId, format, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "reader"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read the deposit.

Step 3. If json, output the deposit. If provo, export to PROV-O. If turtle, serialize to Turtle.

Step 4. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 5. Return the output and the format.

7.9 Bulk Import
function bulkImport(file, provenance, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "depositor"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Parse the file.

Step 3. For each claim, call createHistoricalClaim.

Step 4. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 5. Return the results and the count.

7.10 Bulk Export
function bulkExport(query, format, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "reader"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read the matching claims.

Step 3. If json, output the list. If jsonl, output one line per claim. If provo, export each one.

Step 4. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 5. Return the output and the count.

7.11 Moderate Historical Claim
function moderateHistoricalClaim(claimId, moderationStatus, moderationNotes, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "moderator"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read the existing claim. If null, return an error.

Step 3. Update the moderation status. Insert a moderation record.

Step 4. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 5. Return the claim_id and the status.

7.12 Claim Map
function claimMap(auth, options):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "reader"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read all claims.

Step 3. Build the map with periods as axes and regions as positions.

Step 4. Return the map.

7.13 Claim Timeline
function claimTimeline(claimId, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "reader"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read the claim. If null, return an error.

Step 3. Read the revisions.

Step 4. Build the timeline with the revisions over time.

Step 5. Return the timeline.

